    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Understanding API Documentation\r\n\r\nSkim the documentation for the Open Weather app [here](https://drive.google.com/file/d/14YM40Rev-of7TaPwllaDE7-QvJMI-AgM/view?usp=drive_link). \r\n\r\nUpload the PDF of the API documentation to AI Chat from the library by clicking the `add file` button in the prompt box. Then use AI to answer the questions below.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n1️⃣ What kinds of information does this API provide about the weather?\r\n\r\nList at least three different types of data you notice.\r\n\r\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div> <details style=\"background-color: #4f5b68; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;\"> <summary style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; color: #ffffff;\">💡 Quick check</summary> <div style=\"margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; margin-bottom:75px;\"> <p style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #ffffff;\"> This API provides multiple types of weather data, including <strong>temperature</strong>, <strong>humidity</strong>, <strong>wind</strong>, <strong>weather conditions</strong> (like rain or clouds), and <strong>location information</strong>. Not all of this data needs to be shown in an app, but it’s available if needed. </p> </div> </details>\r\n\r\n\r\n2️⃣ What parameters do you need to set to get weather for a specific location?\r\n\r\nWhich ones are required, and what are they used for?\r\n\r\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div> <details style=\"background-color: #4f5b68; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;\"> <summary style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; color: #ffffff;\">💡 Quick check</summary> <div style=\"margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; margin-bottom:75px;\"> <p style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #ffffff;\"> To get weather for a specific location, the API requires <strong>latitude (lat)</strong> and <strong>longitude (lon)</strong>. These coordinates tell the API exactly where to look. The request also requires an <strong>API key (appid)</strong> to identify who is making the request. </p> </div> </details>\r\n\r\n3️⃣ What unit is the <code>temp</code> value in by default, and how could you change it?\r\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div> <details style=\"background-color: #4f5b68; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;\"> <summary style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; color: #ffffff;\">💡 Quick check</summary> <div style=\"margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; margin-bottom:75px;\"> <p style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #ffffff;\"> By default, <strong>temperature values are in Kelvin</strong>. You can change the unit by using the optional <strong>units</strong> parameter, such as <strong>metric</strong> for Celsius or <strong>imperial</strong> for Fahrenheit. </p> </div> </details>",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "submittable": "false",
